div.p:
Noting that no proposal concerning the breadth of
                    the territorial sea or fishing rights in a contiguous zone received the
                    two-thirds majority required for adoption by the Conference;

Considering, however, that both of these important
                    matters were extensively discussed at the Conference so that nations are fully
                    cognizant of each other’s problems with respect thereto;

list.item:
Requests the Secretary-General to convoke the
                        conference in August, 1959 or as soon thereafter as possible,
                        at________;

Requests the Secretary-General to invite
                        specialized agencies and inter-governmental bodies concerned with the
                        matters to be considered to send observers to the conference;
